# 📊 Basic Data Types

| Data Type | Description           | Example |
| --------- | --------------------- | ------- |
| int       | Whole numbers         | 10      |
| float32   | Decimal numbers       | 10.5    |
| float64   | Large decimal numbers | 99.99   |
| string    | Text                  | "Hello" |
| bool      | True or False         | true    |

---

# 📦 Zero Values

If a variable is not initialized, Go assigns a default value.

| Data Type | Default Value |
| --------- | ------------- |
| int       | 0             |
| float64   | 0.0           |
| string    | ""            |
| bool      | false         |

Example:

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    var a int
    var b float64
    var c string
    var d bool

    fmt.Println(a)
    fmt.Println(b)
    fmt.Println(c)
    fmt.Println(d)
}
```

---

# 🔄 Type Conversion

Go does not support automatic type conversion.

```go
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    var a int = 10
    var b float64 = float64(a)

    fmt.Println(b)
}
```

